title: POST /repos/:repo/calibrate-threshold
tags: [[HTTP endpoint]] Storage
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: Measures the mass-write threshold of each kind of write on a throwaway store, as a background task; sets them when asked.

Asynchronous: `202 Accepted` with `{"task_id": "<32hex>"}`, `400` for a store of fewer
than 100 records (refused before any task), `409 Conflict` when a calibration is
already pending or running for this repository. Follow it through the [[Task endpoints]]; it is cancellable, and a cancelled one writes nothing.

|!Key |!Default |!Meaning |
|`records` |`100000` |the records of the throwaway store |
|`write` |`false` |write the thresholds into `config.json`, in force at once |

The task's result:

```
{"records": 100000, "written": false,
 "thresholds": {"add": 49, "remove": 19, "set": 49, "delete": 9},
 "kinds": [{"kind": "add", "threshold": 49, "reached": true,
            "samples": [{"records": 1, "each_ms": 14.2, "mass_ms": 12.0}, …]}, …]}
```

`reached` is false when no size measured made the bulk write pay; the threshold is
then the largest size measured ([[Calibrating the mass-write thresholds]]). The
thresholds in force are in `GET /repos/:repo` (`mass_write_thresholds`). Additive on
the wire: no `API_VERSION` bump.
